    {
      "fragment_type": "design_rationale",
      "content": "Acceleration factor calculation: For electronic products, activation energy Ea = 0.8 eV. Ts = normal temperature 25℃ + 273 = 298K; Tu = high temperature 40℃ + 273 = 313K; k = Boltzmann constant = 8.62×10⁻⁵ eV/K; RHs = 50% RH (normal use); RHu = 95% RH (accelerated stress); n = humidity acceleration rate constant = 2. Calculated AF = 16.058. Test time calculation uses the Weibull Distribution and Binomial Distribution Synthesis formula with β = 1.5 and sample size = 1.",
